    <h2 id="about-title">An engineering leader who pairs distributed-systems depth with documented business impact, and still ships the systems myself.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="about-body">
    <p>Eleven years at Apple, Amazon, Microsoft, and Susquehanna International Group, from writing the code to running the team that writes it. <a href="/leadership#apple-experience">My Apple experience</a> connects the people, platforms, and operating scope.</p>
    <p>The record: $40M a year taken out of Alexa's data-mining costs at Amazon, with model accuracy up 40%.</p>
    <p>I earned a Wharton Executive MBA with five majors while running the Apple team, and I publish what the two jobs taught me: a framework for measuring enterprise AI return on SSRN, and a paper on who trains senior engineers once AI writes the junior code. At the Praxtera AI Institute I teach executives from HP, Morgan Lewis, PBS, and the Philadelphia Eagles how to govern AI spend.</p>
    <p>I still write production code: four independent products, from schema to app store, and 54 public repositories.</p>
  </div>
